From ab72b5c35e84684ef33dc65c19a56b1dbc4908f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wyze3306 <contact.wyze3306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:49:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] msixvc: walk the NTFS metadata through a block cache

`run` and `streaming` find the files of a package without a segment table
by walking its NTFS metadata, which the ntfs crate reads a file record at a
time through XvdStream, and XvdStream asks for the stream position before
every read. The reader under it is a SyncIoBridge on a tokio file, so each
read and each position query was a task on tokio's blocking pool: for a
Minecraft package (12 898 files) 31 000 reads of 4 KiB, 60 000 seeks and
390 000 futex calls, 0.8 s of every launch.

Put a cache of 256 KiB blocks under XvdStream. It reads the package a block
at a time, keeps the sixteen most recent, and answers seeks and position
queries without touching the reader. The walk itself is unchanged: on six
Minecraft and Minecraft Preview packages, 1.26.52 to 1.26.70, it finds the
same files at the same offsets with the same hashes, in 0.07 to 0.16 s.
---
 crates/msixvc/src/xvd.rs | 193 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 191 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/msixvc/src/xvd.rs b/crates/msixvc/src/xvd.rs
index 79344a7..3967647 100644
--- a/crates/msixvc/src/xvd.rs
+++ b/crates/msixvc/src/xvd.rs
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 use std::cmp::min;
-use std::collections::HashMap;
+use std::collections::{HashMap, VecDeque};
 use std::fmt::Debug;
 use std::io::{self, Error, ErrorKind, Read, Seek, SeekFrom, Write};
 
@@ -172,6 +172,107 @@ impl Debug for XvdEncryptionInfo {
